   "source": {
    "label": "th:2",
    "number": "Theorem (th:2)",
    "quote": "For all models $\\cD$, for all strategies $\\psi$ that are smarter than the uniform strategy on $\\cD$, for all bandit problems~$\\unu$, for all arms $a$, for all $T \\geq 1$, \\[ \\E_{\\unu} \\bigl[ N_{\\psi,a}(T) \\bigr] \\geq \\frac{T}{K} \\Bigl( 1 - \\sqrt{2 T \\Kinf(\\nu_a,\\mu^\\star,\\cD)} \\Bigr)\\,. \\] In particular, \\[ \\forall \\, T \\leq \\frac{1}{8 \\Kinf(\\nu_a,\\mu^\\star,\\cD)}, \\quad \\E_{\\unu} \\bigl[ N_{\\psi,a}(T) \\bigr] \\geq \\frac{T}{2K}\\,. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Pull-count lower bound for each arm a (initial linear regime)."
  },
