   "source": {
    "label": "th:3",
    "number": "Theorem (th:3)",
    "quote": "For all models $\\cD$, for all strategies $\\psi$ that are pairwise symmetric for optimal arms on $\\cD$, for all bandit problems $\\unu$ in $\\cD$, for all suboptimal arms $a$ and all optimal arms $a^\\star$, for all $T \\geq 1$, either $\\E_{\\unu}[N_{\\psi,a}(T)] \\geq \\frac{T}{K}$ or $\\E_{\\unu}[\\max\\{N_{\\psi,a}(T),1\\}/\\max\\{N_{\\psi,a^\\star}(T),1\\}] \\geq 1 - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{2T \\, \\KL(\\nu_a,\\nu_{a^\\star})}{K}}$."
